# SRG-APP-000225-WSR-000141  -  CAT II
# The web server must provide a clustering capability.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000225-WSR-000141
group:           V-206406
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-001190
control_rev5:    SC-24

contribution:    Splunk Enterprise provides the clustering capability this requirement asks
                 for: server.conf configures index clustering, where an instance operates
                 as a cluster manager, peer or search head with a replication factor, and
                 search head clustering, where members share a management URI list and
                 replicate search artifacts. The capability is present in the product;
                 whether it is turned on is an availability decision about this deployment.

external:        Whether this instance is designated a high-availability server, which
                 determines whether the requirement applies at all - system security plan
                 and organizational availability decision
external:        The site's high-availability architecture, including the number of peers,
                 the replication and search factors chosen, and any load balancer in front
                 of the search tier - deployment architecture
external:        Failover of components outside Splunk, such as storage and network paths -
                 infrastructure

manual_reason:   The requirement is that the product provide a clustering capability, and
                 the check makes the rule not applicable where the server is not a
                 high-availability server. Splunk Enterprise provides both index clustering
                 and search head clustering, so the application's share is met by product
                 design. Whether this instance is designated high availability cannot be
                 established from configuration, and a condition requiring [clustering]
                 mode to be other than "disabled" would fail a correctly built
                 single-instance deployment - a false finding against the application.

citation:        server.conf.spec:2432-2438 ([clustering] mode =
                 [manager|peer|searchhead|disabled], "Sets operational mode for this
                 cluster node", default disabled); server.conf.spec:2443-2449
                 (manager_uri); server.conf.spec:2468-2474 (manager_switchover_mode =
                 [disabled|auto|manual], cluster manager redundancy);
                 server.conf.spec:2929-2935 ([clustering] replication_factor, default 3);
                 server.conf.spec:4479-4482 ([shclustering] servers_list);
                 server.conf.spec:4534-4537 ([shclustering] replication_factor, default 3);
                 server.conf.spec:4087 and :5137 ([replication_port://<port>] and
                 [replication_port-ssl://<port>])
finding:         Not decidable from Splunk configuration: Splunk Enterprise provides both
                 index clustering and search head clustering, so the capability this
                 requirement asks for exists in the product; whether clustering must be
                 enabled follows from the system's high-availability designation, which is
                 recorded outside the application.
